A provider's injector input is an interface whose method returns a type that does
not type-check (Missing is undefined). The invalid type is buried inside the
interface method signature, not at the top level; the loader tolerates the type
error, but plumb must still reject rather than emit an interface containing the
unprintable "invalid type". (The invalid-type walk descends into interface method
signatures; a walk that stopped at the interface would let this reach the emitter,
where formatting panics.)
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidType
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Thing struct{}

//plumb:build
func Use(r interface{ Read() Missing }) *Thing { return &Thing{} }
